{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויקרא יעקב לבניו", :translit "vayikra ya'akov livnotav", :gloss "And Jacob called to his sons"} {:he "שרצה לגלות להם הקץ ונסתם ממנו", :translit "she'ratzah legalot lahem haketz venistam mimenu", :gloss "that he wished to reveal to them the End but it was hidden from him"} {:he "אמר יעקב שמא יש בכם חטא", :translit "amar ya'akov ulai yesh bachem chet", :gloss "Jacob said perhaps there is sin among you"} {:he "אמרו לו תדקדק בשמותינו ולא תמצא בהם אותיות חט", :translit "amru lo tadkek bishmotainu velo timtza bahem otiyot chet tet", :gloss "they said to him examine our names and you will not find in them the letters chet tet"} {:he "אמר להם גם אין בהם אותיות קץ", :translit "amar lahem gam ein bahem otiyot kuf tzadi", :gloss "he said to them also the letters kuf tzadi are not in them"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Absence of the letters ח״ט from all twelve tribal names taken as proof of no sin"} {:kind :other, :note "Absence of the letters ק״ץ from all twelve tribal names taken as sign the End remains hidden"}], :frame {:text "Jacob wished to reveal the time of the End to his sons but it was hidden from him, as taught in Pesachim 56a. He suspected sin among them, but they directed him to examine their names and find no letters spelling חט. Pesachim 56a records that Jacob sought to reveal the End but it departed from him.", :sources ["Pesachim 56a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Absence of the letters ח״ט from all twelve tribal names taken as proof of no sin", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Absence of the letters ק״ץ from all twelve tribal names taken as sign the End remains hidden", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:12:10.641611752Z", :model "glm-5.2"}